  "summary_en": "European Commission report presenting the interim evaluation of the Digital Europe Programme (EUR 8.16bn, 2021-2027) across HPC, AI, cybersecurity, skills, digital adoption and semiconductors. It finds the programme relevant and effective, notes co-funding and security-restriction burdens, and feeds into the proposed European Competitiveness Fund. Robotics appears only in passing.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Programme judged highly relevant, effective and flexible across six specific objectives.",
   "Funded AI Testing and Experimentation Facilities, AI factories and tools supporting AI Act compliance.",
   "Challenges: 50% co-financing, State aid and funding-combination complexity, ownership-control assessments.",
   "Draghi report cited: EU digital dependency and regulatory burden hamper competitiveness.",
   "Lessons to inform the proposed European Competitiveness Fund in the next MFF."
